<title>UK: ABN-AMRO in London wins August Reuter forex poll.</title>
<headline>ABN-AMRO in London wins August Reuter forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN-AMRO in London won the August Reuter foreign exchange poll, with an average divergence rate of 0.34 percent beating 32 other contenders from across the globe in the monthly contest.</p>
<p>In second place was Chase Investment Bank, London with 0.428 percent followed by DKB, also in London, with a 0.519 percent divergence rate.</p>
<p>Overall, the percentage difference between actual and forecasted rates varied between 0.335 and 3.455 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on August 29 of dollar/mark at 1.4777 marks, dollar/yen at 108.62 yen and sterling/dollar at $1.5630.</p>
<p>The following are the top 20 forecasters and their predictions.</p>
